# /etc/init: what init starts once the console, disk and file servers,
# which it needs to read this, are up (docs/kernel.md, The shell).
#
# A line names a server, by the name it registers: init starts it, and
# what it needs, in its own order. Or it names a program file, by its
# path, and its arguments: init starts it with the console as standard
# output and error, starts it again if it faults or is killed, and lets
# it be once it exits. The shell starts after them all.

